{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren","id":702253,"title":"Gaian answer to Yeren?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-15T09:55:15-07:00","id":702253,"title":"Gaian answer to Yeren?","content":"A proto-shifter has been created by the Wyrm, is there any reason Gaia can't make new reinforcements as well? Perhaps a new version of Apis? Or has she used up whatever juice she had in creating the original shapeshifters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T10:11:45-07:00","id":702286,"title":"","content":"All the true Fera (not mockery breeds) were created with a distinct purpose long ago by Gaia. What reason would these new beings have for existing? Momma Gaia doesn't just gin up new/extinct breeds just to cover for the mistakes made during the Wars of Rage and the War of Tears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T10:21:13-07:00","id":702291,"title":"","content":"Who says she isn't? Depending on what you believe, every new Kami could potentially become a new breed. Some do believe that she doesn't have the juice anymore though, that is why her last children, the Kitsune, are so much weaker then the other breeds. I think if she wanted to bring back any of the lost shifters she would just guide the ones lost in the umbra back to the material plane, less effort and just as effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T11:58:36-07:00","id":702382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=702286#post702286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the true Fera (not mockery breeds) were created with a distinct purpose long ago by Gaia. What reason would these new beings have for existing? Momma Gaia doesn't just gin up new/extinct breeds just to cover for the mistakes made during the Wars of Rage and the War of Tears.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if her life depends on it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T12:44:02-07:00","id":702443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=702382#post702382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if her life depends on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It already does, doesn't it? It's not looking very good at the Apocalypse front, so if Gaia doesn't act now, that means she either has no power or no will to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T14:15:47-07:00","id":702518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=702382#post702382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if her life depends on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been on the line for ages now. Alas, Gaia is gone. She's silent and doesn't respond to summonings. Her avatars can only be encountered in a couple of lost realms that are nigh impossible to get to, and she hasn't spoken with anyone directly in ages. The concept of her actually being involved with the Apocalypse War is nigh unthinkable, and the popular theory among the Garou is that she has been wounded so badly that she has curled up in pain and cannot really get back to the game in time. The Black Spiral Dancers know that she has given up and curled up to die. They will gladly end her once and for all.<br /> <br /> tl:dr, Gaia's a non issue and she's not gonna be affecting anything unless the PC's pull something insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T16:53:47-07:00","id":702621,"title":"","content":"Side note, if vtm4th is after Gehenna, and by that idea werewolf 4th after the apocalypse... Would gaia then remake fera? Or would it just be whoevers left?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T17:20:08-07:00","id":702683,"title":"","content":"I don't believe the Kitsune are actually 'weaker' as far as Gaia is concerned - she makes the breeds for her own reasons, and there's no reason to doubt her competence in making them as fit for purpose as each other.<br /> <br /> Of course, the breeds themselves don't have perfect understanding of Gaia's motives, or plans, or reasoning - so they guess, and those guesses lead to ideas such as 'kitsune are weaker than other breeds'. But it's an invalid comparison - like saying Garou are weaker than Rokea because they drown, or weaker than mokole because they don't have mnesis.<br /> <br /> So, on topic, there's no canon reason Gaia couldn't make a new Breed tomorrow, if she had a need for it. And it would be no weaker than any others - barring some time required to learn all their Gifts and ways to raise renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T17:48:38-07:00","id":702728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=702518#post702518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tl:dr, Gaia's a non issue and she's not gonna be affecting anything unless the PC's pull something insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly right, and it is really necessary for any sort of story that doesn't resemble Exalted to take place. Gaia being removed as a factor is really what you have to do in order to have conflict. The struggle against the Wyrm totally changes if Gaia can just make more Fera/fix whatever is broken. The desperate, last-ditch narrative is replaced by something else, a world where the actions of the Garou (and the players!) are tertiary at best as the primary problems and complications of the setting are fixed via Deus ex Machina.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-15-2015, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T18:16:47-07:00","id":702764,"title":"","content":"oh Speaking of &quot;Resemble exalted&quot; I experimented with the 'wyld world' suggested in &quot;Book of the wyld&quot; but it kept feeling like Exalted<br /> <br /> Thoughts on how it could feel any other way?<br /> <br /> another thing<br /> <br /> if The lost breeds return any idea on what the reprecussions would be?<br /> <br /> The Apis coming back things Like blessing of Hathor would let them enhaonce the changing breeds populations...<br /> <br /> The Grondr can cleanse the earrth of poisons...<br /> <br /> No idea What reprecussions the Camazotz returning would have beyond the purely political.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T18:30:19-07:00","id":702789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=702683#post702683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe the Kitsune are actually 'weaker' as far as Gaia is concerned - she makes the breeds for her own reasons, and there's no reason to doubt her competence in making them as fit for purpose as each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Rokea and the Mokole are stronger, and Gaia didn't make them. The Wyld created them both as a gift to Gaia. They have innate abilities that are much stronger then their cousins such as the ability to live forever if not killed and a spiritual genetic memory that allows them remember a great history. The Kitsune inability to breed properly resulting in the death of one or both of it parents and the further inability to heal properly most definitely make them weaker.<br /> <br /> As Asmodai stated, there is plenty of reason that she can't create any more shifters. She can barely muster the strength to guide her current children and to create lesser Kami, let alone something of spiritual strength even on par with an Anurana. As far as most the stories and rules go, she down for count and it doesn't look like shes getting up.<br /> <br /> That said, if it fits your story and you want to go that way then you should definitely do it. It just doesn't feel right to me, and as always, that is simply my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T19:20:50-07:00","id":702868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=702789#post702789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Rokea and the Mokole are stronger, and Gaia didn't make them. The Wyld created them both as a gift to Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gvdf5n-zI14\" data-code=\"gvdf5n-zI14\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/gvdf5n-zI14/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> The Mokole, at the very least, were produced by Gaia. The Undersea Triat thing is an odd fixture that doesn't really support not being made by Gaia, since it gets confused and refers to them as mere Incarnae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T21:52:11-07:00","id":702996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=702789#post702789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kitsune inability to breed properly resulting in the death of one or both of it parents and the further inability to heal properly most definitely make them weaker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that's actually part of what she needs them for. Perhaps if they didn't face such sorrow at every new Kitsune, they would be tempted to overpopulate, or grow proud of having multiple shapeshifting children where such hubris would be counter-productive to Gaia's need.<br /> <br /> My point is, we don't know, and the Breeds definitely don't know - they have their own biases and errors when making judgment calls.<br /> <br /> (Not that it can't be fun to discuss though, like now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T22:03:43-07:00","id":703001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=702996#post702996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or that's actually part of what she needs them for. Perhaps if they didn't face such sorrow at every new Kitsune, they would be tempted to overpopulate, or grow proud of having multiple shapeshifting children where such hubris would be counter-productive to Gaia's need.<br /> <br /> My point is, we don't know, and the Breeds definitely don't know - they have their own biases and errors when making judgment calls.<br /> <br /> (Not that it can't be fun to discuss though, like now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, foxes can be really, really long-lived, since lifespan doubles with each extra tail. An elder with five tails has a lifespan of roughly 60 x 2^4, or 1,920 years, as a very conservative estimate. Given that it's modifying a changing breed's lifespan, it's probably closer to double that, if not a bit more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T02:29:58-07:00","id":703126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=702789#post702789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Rokea and the Mokole are stronger, and Gaia didn't make them. The Wyld created them both as a gift to Gaia. They have innate abilities that are much stronger then their cousins such as the ability to live forever if not killed and a spiritual genetic memory that allows them remember a great history. The Kitsune inability to breed properly resulting in the death of one or both of it parents and the further inability to heal properly most definitely make them weaker.<br /> <br /> As Asmodai stated, there is plenty of reason that she can't create any more shifters. She can barely muster the strength to guide her current children and to create lesser Kami, let alone something of spiritual strength even on par with an Anurana. As far as most the stories and rules go, she down for count and it doesn't look like shes getting up.<br /> <br /> That said, if it fits your story and you want to go that way then you should definitely do it. It just doesn't feel right to me, and as always, that is simply my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stronger is relative. All the breeds have their uses and benefits and cannot be compared like that. Physical power is not the be and all of Werewolf, it's a point that's constantly reiterated by the game. Besides, Gaia made both the Mokole and the Rokea. Just because they have slightly different legendry does not change that they were all her chosen created for different roles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T04:41:27-07:00","id":703194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren#post702253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A proto-shifter has been created by the Wyrm, is there any reason Gaia can't make new reinforcements as well? Perhaps a new version of Apis? Or has she used up whatever juice she had in creating the original shapeshifters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where, how and what it is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T05:01:20-07:00","id":703209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=703126#post703126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stronger is relative. All the breeds have their uses and benefits and cannot be compared like that. Physical power is not the be and all of Werewolf, it's a point that's constantly reiterated by the game. Besides, Gaia made both the Mokole and the Rokea. Just because they have slightly different legendry does not change that they were all her chosen created for different roles.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the opening of the Mokole book it talks about how the Wyld created the Mokole and the Rokea to protect Gaia. The Weaver, not wanting to be shown up, created the Insect-shifters to do the same but then used them to try to control her. Queen Ananasi created the Ananasi to remove the other insect breeds (hence the Insect Wars from prehistory) and try to bring balance back to the trait. Gaia is not the only being that can create shifters, she is just the one with the most need to do so hence so many others were created later.<br /> <br /> As Gaia's memory I consider these tales to be history not legend, to each there own though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T06:01:18-07:00","id":703265,"title":"","content":"History and legend is pretty damn muddled with oral cultures, you know. The Mokole cannot remember that point in time, since their memories of the Dragon Kings are muddled, let alone anything before that. What they know for sure is that they and the Rokea were around the longest. Since both of these are servants of Gaia and work on the same principles as Gaian shifters they were probably created by her. Of course, one thing that's not consistent between the breeds is their past and their cosmic priorities. They all agree that they are there for Gaia (except for Ananasi who are there for Ananasa), the rest is all rather up in the air.<br /> <br /> For instance, who is more powerful, the Triat or Gaia? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T06:38:41-07:00","id":703346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=703194#post703194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where, how and what it is?</div> </div> </div> </div>The W20 Book of the Wyrm introduces Mockery Breeds - Pentex' own attempts at creating something like Shapeshifters. The most succesful try so far are the Yeren, sociopathic apeshifters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T06:58:43-07:00","id":703367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=703346#post703346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The W20 Book of the Wyrm introduces Mockery Breeds - Pentex' own attempts at creating something like Shapeshifters. The most succesful try so far are the Yeren, sociopathic apeshifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm, curious, but i get the feeling Pentex might be seriously behind the competition when it comes to that sector... :P<br /> <br /> As an aside, it says much of internal politics that they would invest in several experiments with creating a whole new shapeshifter instead of expanding on Alred's Skin Dancer project in the Amazon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah, it blew up big time, twice even, but that was more due Samuel Haight's unreliability than any actual failure of concept! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T07:20:13-07:00","id":703395,"title":"","content":"Alred's Skin Dancer project in the Amazon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T07:35:04-07:00","id":703409,"title":"","content":"Gaia knows not to waste time on another breed Garou will just murder for being different.<br /> <br /> On Kitsune power: Kitsune buy &quot;unfavored&quot; gifts at the same cost as favored. The only gifts that are impossible for them to learn from others are ones that require shapes they cannot take. KItsune have their own whole damned Magic type. KItsune can learn Hedge Magic. Kitsune can Soak SIlver Damage and it counts as Lethal for them(this is important because of all sorts of healing magics). KItsune are the only breed which has more than 6 ranks.<br /> <br /> Its kind of obvious Kitsune were meant to be Gaia's super magic breed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T07:55:24-07:00","id":703453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=703395#post703395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alred's Skin Dancer project in the Amazon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Robert Alred, one of Pentex's bigwigs in the original Book of the Wyrm, also happens to be garou kinfolk and have had some association with Samuel Haight, enough of it that they masterminded the idea of making a &quot;Skin Dancer&quot; tribe out of converting other kinfolk resentful of their garou relatives through the same ritual Sam used on himself and planned to use the already ongoing violence between Pentex and the shapeshifters in Amazon as cover for all the killing involved in collecting the garou pelts necessary to make them.<br /> <br /> A simple plan, until Haight got his hands in some awakened artifact and got in his crazy head this wacky idea of taking down a Dreamspeaker oracle and stealing his avatar and things went the way of the dodo from there mostly...<br /> <br /> It's left quite unclear if Alred was himself turned into a Skin Dancer before the Eldorado debacle or learned the ritual himself, but it wouldn't be far-fetched for Sam to do either thing, for financial support and someone to &quot;continue his dream&quot; in case he died.<br /> <br /> Though most of that hinges on Samuel's sincerity about the desire to make this &quot;anti-tribe&quot;, obviously - it <b>could</b> have been a ploy on a highly individualistic madman part to get a comfy position and almost lmitless financial support from Pentex for his insane personal power trip projects all along...<br /> It all depends on how much weight one gives to &quot;Outcasts&quot;, a book that might be of debatable canonicity anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-16-2015, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T08:19:15-07:00","id":703487,"title":"","content":"I always liked the stuff from Outcasts on the Skin Dancers. It gave a post-Haight prospective of the &quot;tribes&quot; society. I never heard the part about Robert Alerd and Haight's plans in the Amazon. I doubt he ever reaped the benefits of the ritual as we never hear anything about him after the fact in Outcasts or the later SAS:Skinner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T09:31:22-07:00","id":703597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=703487#post703487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always liked the stuff from Outcasts on the Skin Dancers. It gave a post-Haight prospective of the &quot;tribes&quot; society. I never heard the part about Robert Alerd and Haight's plans in the Amazon. I doubt he ever reaped the benefits of the ritual as we never hear anything about him after the fact in Outcasts or the later SAS:Skinner.</div> </div> </div> </div>As i said, it could go either way - truth be told the silence on Alred is glaring to say the least, considering the original mention of the Skin Dancers as a concept back in Rage Across Amazon is strongly tied on Samuel getting Pentex's support through him to actually make it feasible. And as i said, some groups might be more interested in Sam as individual madman that goes too far than the Skin Dancers as anti-tribe per se.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T14:08:53-07:00","id":703783,"title":"","content":"@Baaldam<br /> The problem with the whole Skindancer stuff is that it takes five Garou, killed under very specific circumstances, to create one Skindancer. It's a nice by-product of something you were going to do anyway, but it's not particularly doable on a massive scale. Mockery breeds, on the other hand side, might well be suitable for mass-production - or they might not be, but you don't know until you've tried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T16:15:50-07:00","id":703925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=703783#post703783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Baaldam<br /> The problem with the whole Skindancer stuff is that it takes five Garou, killed under very specific circumstances, to create one Skindancer. It's a nice by-product of something you were going to do anyway, but it's not particularly doable on a massive scale. Mockery breeds, on the other hand side, might well be suitable for mass-production - or they might not be, but you don't know until you've tried.</div> </div> </div> </div>Main reason why Alred came with the scheme to exploit an ongoing attrition war like the one Pentex has with the Fera in the Amazon to, if not mass produce, at least do it in considerable numbers. That said killing a number of garou ritually and guarding their skins for future could take less time logistically than gods only know how long it takes to literally brew a new shapeshifter basically from scratch, without even going into failures, false starts and such.<br /> <br /> With the Skin Dancer methodology even when not making a new member you are <b>still</b> killing garou anyway. Not to mention someone at Pentex could experiment with using a bunch of kinfolk to try and cook up a more technological and - hopefully - less laborious variant of Samuel Haight's process, as mentioned previously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T03:22:12-07:00","id":704623,"title":"","content":"Considering how many Garou you need to kill, how dangerous they are and how rare they are, it just feels very contrived that there is more then 3-4 Skindancers in the whole world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T10:01:34-07:00","id":705298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=704623#post704623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how many Garou you need to kill, how dangerous they are and how rare they are, it just feels very contrived that there is more then 3-4 Skindancers in the whole world.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet someone thinks that making an army of tube-grown artificial shapeshifters is an important and more pratical step in dealing with their threat, that is supposed to be less contrived and more pratical somehow, eh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T10:09:15-07:00","id":705330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=705298#post705298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yet someone thinks that making an army of tube-grown artificial shapeshifters is an important and more pratical step in dealing with their threat, that is supposed to be less contrived and more pratical somehow, eh?</div> </div> </div> </div>In that it's much less resource intensive than trying to get five perfectly preserved pelts on the same phase of the moon from beings that can rip you a new one and might result in more successes like the Yeren that could be used to recruit and empower future operatives? Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T11:08:24-07:00","id":705481,"title":"","content":"Back sort of on topic isn't Cockroach trying to steal the Wereroaches for gaia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"