\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=705601#post705601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Cockroach is looking out for Cockroach, not Gaia. He just wants more power so that he can do what he does best, survive. This may or may not benefit Gaia as Cockroach would jump teams faster then any of the other totems if it meant that he gets to continue on.</div> </div> </div> </div>After all only Twinkies and cockroaches will survive a nuclear war....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T06:50:31-07:00","id":706715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=705330#post705330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In that it's much less resource intensive than trying to get five perfectly preserved pelts on the same phase of the moon from beings that can rip you a new one and might result in more successes like the Yeren that could be used to recruit and empower future operatives? Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things that you are already fighting and coming after your interests anyway? Sure... As i said, even when not collecting the skins you are grinding the competition, so you are getting something out of the investiment either way, not to mention other far more ruthless tactics one may work with to increase one's chances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=705508#post705508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please check the requirements for one activity and who is performing it and the other activity and who is performing it and get back to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering we are speaking of magic and weird science, it's pretty much ST fiat either way, no? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T07:33:24-07:00","id":706820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=706715#post706715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Things that you are already fighting and coming after your interests anyway? Sure... As i said, even when not collecting the skins you are grinding the competition, so you are getting something out of the investiment either way, not to mention other far more ruthless tactics one may work with to increase one's chances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting more ruthless tends to increase the possibility that you won't get the skins in the proper condition, because they'll be full of holes from silver bullets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Considering we are speaking of magic and weird science, it's pretty much ST fiat either way, no? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>STs who pull too much fiat can end up with lost players, so it might pay off to try and fiat softly, going with the flow to smooth over problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T08:12:08-07:00","id":708758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=706820#post706820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Getting more ruthless tends to increase the possibility that you won't get the skins in the proper condition, because they'll be full of holes from silver bullets.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but only a problem if killing the garou per se wasn't also to Pentex's benefit anyway. Not like hunting them down for skins didn't run in much the same risks. It's basically a matter of taking some extra from the usual garou-killing operations that are in fact already a need for the corp's continued survival, while the lab work gives you little or nothing while gobbling revenue until something - that might or not be effective - comes out, after years or decades of experimentation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=706820#post706820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">STs who pull too much fiat can end up with lost players, so it might pay off to try and fiat softly, going with the flow to smooth over problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on the people involved. Personally making anything in vitro and hope for any results in anything less than a decade - not even speaking of <b>practical</b> results - breaks <b>my</b> suspension of disbelief, what to say of producing whole gangs to effectively use against the several fera.<br /> <br /> Whoa, wait - an alternative that might be better than either: lunatic breeding.<br /> <br /> Capture lots of wolves, as many as one can, put them in a special reserve or zoo.<br /> <br /> Try to identify those who would be kinfolk - actual tribal stock not important as long as they are kinfolk - separate them in couples and get them to breed as frequently as they can with good access to food &amp; etc.<br /> <br /> Most of them will be kinfolk too, but as wolves usually birth in litters of 5-6 pups, occasions of one breeding true as lupus will appear much more frequently than among homids. Not to mention they usually take only an year or two to go through first change in comparison to the 12+ years of a homid.<br /> <br /> Turn these sheltered &quot;lunatic wolves&quot; over to the Black Spirals for conversion or, if one finds the members of that tribe too crazy and unreliable, experiment with educating them inside Pentex itself, making a tribe of &quot;corporate wolves&quot; more in synch with their own interests.<br /> <br /> Steal your enemies' future and make it into your shock troops. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-19-2015, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T10:50:43-07:00","id":708993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True, but only a problem if killing the garou per se wasn't also to Pentex's benefit anyway. Not like hunting them down for skins didn't run in much the same risks. It's basically a matter of taking some extra from the usual garou-killing operations that are in fact already a need for the corp's continued survival, while the lab work gives you little or nothing while gobbling revenue until something - that might or not be effective - comes out, after years or decades of experimentation. </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. Killing Garou is necessary, but killing them for their furs may often mean holding back - which is really not something that you want to do when confronted by them, particularly in regions with no other witnesses. There, you want to shred them with grenades, pour out the napalm and generally do stuff with them that may make them die young, but probably won't leave a good-looking corpse.<br /> Thus, the opportunity cost of killing them in Skin Dancer-friendly ways is posssibly not killing them at all or taking greater losses than you would otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T11:09:18-07:00","id":709046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=708993#post708993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no. Killing Garou is necessary, but killing them for their furs may often mean holding back - which is really not something that you want to do when confronted by them, particularly in regions with no other witnesses. There, you want to shred them with grenades, pour out the napalm and generally do stuff with them that may make them die young, but probably won't leave a good-looking corpse.<br /> Thus, the opportunity cost of killing them in Skin Dancer-friendly ways is posssibly not killing them at all or taking greater losses than you would otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or spending some time in devising strategy? Also, not every strike team can count on that level of gear - in fact most of them certainly won't in most situations outside of straight attacking a caern in some secluded place. Moving around serious military-grade gear ain't exaclty a cakewalk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T12:04:25-07:00","id":709132,"title":"","content":"I don't think it is that hard to get the pelt relatively intact. The Ritual of Sacred Rebirth never says that the pelt has to be immaculate. I am sure Minotaur will accept skins with a few burns or bullet holes. The rite is already quite difficult to enact- why get all choosy about the state of the dead Garou's epidermis, especially when it doesn't seem to be a consideration in the rite's description?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T12:06:20-07:00","id":709134,"title":"","content":"And by devising strategy you mean &quot;Adapting your existing strategy to your new additional objective of preserving the enemies' corpses&quot;? Good old mission creep, bane of ground troops everywhere..<br /> Additionally, this can even set a timer on your attacks: If you don't kill a whole pack in one go, you either need an average of 13 kills until you've got 5 matching corpses or you put additional time constraints on your strikes (&quot;We've already got 4 crescent pelts, we need to strike within the next two days or wait about two and a half weeks&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T03:22:53-07:00","id":712133,"title":"","content":"It IS possible that in the distant past, there where Ape shifters...After all, there where insect shifters once upon a time, and now you see a bunch of Samsa running around. Who knows, maybe the Wyrm just corrupted some ancient aspects of Gaia? Could of gotten their hands on a bunch of Mountain Gorillas who still had a spark of that ancient lineage, ripped it inside out, and twisted it to his own designs and dumped the tattered spiritual forces into some power hungry bastard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1645-autochthon","name":"Autochthon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T03:32:56-07:00","id":712139,"title":"","content":"That's definitely a workable idea, though I doubt it would ever be canonically confirmed.<br /> <br /> Perhaps those wereapes are where the human half of werecreatures came from!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T04:46:19-07:00","id":712199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=709132#post709132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it is that hard to get the pelt relatively intact. The Ritual of Sacred Rebirth never says that the pelt has to be immaculate. I am sure Minotaur will accept skins with a few burns or bullet holes. The rite is already quite difficult to enact- why get all choosy about the state of the dead Garou's epidermis, especially when it doesn't seem to be a consideration in the rite's description?</div> </div> </div> </div>Minotaur isn't the one that empowers this ritual so he doesn't really factor in. He didn't become the tribes totem until after Haight died. I agree though that the state of the pelt doesn't need to be in that great of shape, it just needs to be mostly there as it is acting as a conduit more then anything. I know that the furs collected make up the pelt of the new Skin Dancer so with 5 of them I think they have more then enough material for their new hide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=709134#post709134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And by devising strategy you mean &quot;Adapting your existing strategy to your new additional objective of preserving the enemies' corpses&quot;? Good old mission creep, bane of ground troops everywhere..<br /> Additionally, this can even set a timer on your attacks: If you don't kill a whole pack in one go, you either need an average of 13 kills until you've got 5 matching corpses or you put additional time constraints on your strikes (&quot;We've already got 4 crescent pelts, we need to strike within the next two days or wait about two and a half weeks&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets keep in mind that these aren't Pentex soldiers or human Hunters. These guys/gals are Kinfolk, they know how Garou society operate and they know the weaknesses of the tribes. They also take a great deal of time cultivating sympathizers in the Septs that they choose to target, this is evident in the SAS:Skinner. They are also very patient, the Rite of Sacred Rebirth is not the only way that they bring people into the tribe. If you use the information from WoD:Outcasts, they have started taking in Ronin that can't find a place anywhere else. Those Ronin that can be trusted are brought into the fold, the rest are harvested for the next kinfolk brother/sister in line, which allows them a little more control over when that pelt is harvested. Some members of the tribe don't hunt the nation at all. They go after BSD exclusively which means if they are patient they just need to find a nest, alert the local Sept, and then they can just salvage the left overs after a skirmish.<br /> <br /> All that is just taking into account the Kinfolk who side with the Skin Dancers, when you factor into that their are already changed Skin Dancers out their aiding them, that means they really aren't a small or weak force to deal with. Taking what we have from Outcasts, there are 4 camps in the Skin Dancers, each of which is lead by a Skin Dancer that Samuel Haight helped create. From SAS:Skinner we know the Vulture pack had between 5-8 members i believe. If all 4 camps are about the same size then we have between 20-32 Skin Dancers who have already gone through the change or are Ronin who have can welcomed into the tribe. Even on the low end, given that the Garou Nation really pays them no mind, thats plenty to be able to get away with taking pelts here and there as long as they don't get greedy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T07:24:52-07:00","id":712374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/702253-gaian-answer-to-yeren?p=712199#post712199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Minotaur isn't the one that empowers this ritual so he doesn't really factor in. He didn't become the tribes totem until after Haight died. I agree though that the state of the pelt doesn't need to be in that great of shape, it just needs to be mostly there as it is acting as a conduit more then anything. I know that the furs collected make up the pelt of the new Skin Dancer so with 5 of them I think they have more then enough material for their new hide.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be stretched further than strict concerns of matter might account for. Five forms, five skins...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lets keep in mind that these aren't Pentex soldiers or human Hunters. These guys/gals are Kinfolk, they know how Garou society operate and they know the weaknesses of the tribes. They also take a great deal of time cultivating sympathizers in the Septs that they choose to target, this is evident in the SAS:Skinner. They are also very patient, the Rite of Sacred Rebirth is not the only way that they bring people into the tribe. If you use the information from WoD:Outcasts, they have started taking in Ronin that can't find a place anywhere else. Those Ronin that can be trusted are brought into the fold, the rest are harvested for the next kinfolk brother/sister in line, which allows them a little more control over when that pelt is harvested. Some members of the tribe don't hunt the nation at all. They go after BSD exclusively which means if they are patient they just need to find a nest, alert the local Sept, and then they can just salvage the left overs after a skirmish.<br /> <br /> All that is just taking into account the Kinfolk who side with the Skin Dancers, when you factor into that their are already changed Skin Dancers out their aiding them, that means they really aren't a small or weak force to deal with. Taking what we have from Outcasts, there are 4 camps in the Skin Dancers, each of which is lead by a Skin Dancer that Samuel Haight helped create. From SAS:Skinner we know the Vulture pack had between 5-8 members i believe. If all 4 camps are about the same size then we have between 20-32 Skin Dancers who have already gone through the change or are Ronin who have can welcomed into the tribe. Even on the low end, given that the Garou Nation really pays them no mind, thats plenty to be able to get away with taking pelts here and there as long as they don't get greedy. </div> </div> </div>None of this makes taking pelts simple or manageable compared to just going in unrestrained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T08:07:56-07:00","id":712432,"title":"","content":"@Derzhuzad<br /> Ah, I wasn't aware we were talking about Kinfolk acting on their own - but in that case, you'd have a different problem: What use are they to Pentex? They've managed to usurp their powers aided by their tribe and while they may be wyrm-tainted, that confers no automatic kinship to Pentex. In essence, where there was one tribe of potential (and unstable) allies before, there are now two. This doesn't get the company particularly closer to a shifter faction of their own - Project Lycaon does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}